<article class="env-lemma" id="0D4C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D4C">Lemma <span data-tag="0D4C">31.31.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a quasi-coherent graded $\mathcal{O}_ S$-algebra. Let $p : X = \underline{\text{Proj}}_ S(\mathcal{A}) \to S$ be the relative Proj of $\mathcal{A}$. If $\mathcal{A}_ d$ is a flat $\mathcal{O}_ S$-module for $d \gg 0$, then $p$ is flat and $\mathcal{O}_ X(d)$ is flat over $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Affine locally flatness of $X$ over $S$ reduces to the following statement: Let $R$ be a ring, let $A$ be a graded $R$-algebra with $A_ d$ flat over $R$ for $d \gg 0$, let $f \in A_ d$ for some $d > 0$, then $A_{(f)}$ is flat over $R$. Since $A_{(f)} = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits A_{nd}$ where the transition maps are given by multiplication by $f$, this follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/05UT" data-tag="05UT">10.39.3</a>. Argue similarly to get flatness of $\mathcal{O}_ X(d)$ over $S$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>